Found by the secrets worker during k362 (2026-10-31). k362 masks the Hetzner API token in `ocp keys secure`'s one Hetzner error, as `ocp init` does (k265), through `OCP::ErrorLine::one_line($err, mask => $token)` from k342. Other Hetzner callers still print API/LWP errors without masking the token:
- the `ocp apply` bootstrap (lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Bootstrap.pm);
- `ocp destroy`;
- `ocp hetzner list`;
- the OCP::Provider factory (the Hetzner provider's errors).

A WWW::Hetzner/LWP error can carry the request, Authorization header included.

Done = every place OCP prints or dies with an error that came from a Hetzner call masks the token, via one_line with mask, or a die message that already went through it. Find them all (grep the WWW::Hetzner calls) and list them in the note. One test per command, where the fake Hetzner dies with the token in its message; the token appears nowhere on STDOUT/STDERR. Red first, then a mutation check.

Lanes: ocp-provider-worker (factory, Hetzner provider), with the apply/destroy sites in the same patch if they are only the print line (cross-lane edits named in the note).

